      ],
      "statement": "Assume the Cartan datum of [[def-quiver-hecke-klr-algebra-for-a-symmetrizable-cartan-datum]] has symmetric Cartan matrix $a_{ij}=a_{ji}$ and uses the quiver normalization $d_i=1$ for every i, the field $k$ has characteristic $0$, and the KLR parameters are the quiver-geometric ones (the specialization attached to a finite quiver without loops, with arbitrary arrow multiplicities $h_{ij}$ and $a_{ij}=-(h_{ij}+h_{ji})$: $Q_{ij}(u,v)=(-1)^{h_{ij}}(u-v)^{h_{ij}+h_{ji}}$ for $i\\ne j$, in the fixed native crossing-sign convention; arbitrary parameter changes, including a global replacement by $u+v$, require their own proved gauge equivalence). Then, normalizing each indecomposable finitely generated graded projective $R(\\beta)$-module to be self-dual for the contravariant graded projective duality $P^\\#=\\operatorname{HOM}_{R(\\beta)}(P,R(\\beta))^\\psi$ ($P\\cong P^\\#$ after the unique normalizing shift), the map $b\\mapsto[P_b]$ is a bijection between the lower global basis $B(\\infty)$ of the negative half ([[def-lower-global-basis-of-a-quantum-highest-weight-module]], [[thm-existence-bar-invariance-and-uniqueness-of-the-lower-global-basis]]) and the shift-orbit basis of $K_0(R)$ by self-dual indecomposable projectives; under the isomorphism $\\gamma$ of [[thm-klr-categorification-of-the-negative-quantum-half]] one has $\\gamma(G(b))=[P_b]$ for the lower global lift $G(b)$, and the identification is compatible with the based quotient of [[thm-global-basis-projection-from-the-negative-half-to-a-highest-weight-module]]. No extension to arbitrary KLR parameters or to non-symmetric Cartan data is asserted here; any such extension requires its own parameter-change invariance theorem.",
      "strategy": "The only remaining held prerequisite is the SEMISIMPLE QUIVER-FLAG EXT REALIZATION, in the full symmetric d_i=1/characteristic0/loopless-quiver parameter scope including arbitrary edge multiplicities. Construct delta L=sum_nu (pi_nu)!k[dim Ftilde_nu] on E_V; prove its decomposition into shifts of simple equivariant perverse sheaves and the graded isomorphism R(beta)=Ext_G^*(delta L,delta L) with the actual native signs and VV multiplication convention (a*b is categorical b composed with a, so R is the opposite of the ordinary categorical End algebra). VV1.3 assumes semisimple proper pushforward, and its Theorem3.6 uses the Ext/Borel-Moore convolution comparison, localization and affine-paving computation. Those geometric foundations still have no proved local suppliers. BBD6.2.5/6.2.7 imports arithmetic purity; its mere citation is not a local proof. Full ext/flag realization remains held, not weakened to finite ADE or simple edges.\nOnce that realization is proved, no separate equivariant-formality/base-change theorem is needed for this route. The graded Yoneda functor Y_T=Ext_G^*(delta L,T) gives a fully faithful equivalence from add(delta L shifts) to finite graded projective R-modules: verify it on the generator delta L by Hom_R(R,R)=R^op=End_DG(delta L) with ordinary categorical composition, extend to finite sums/shifts, and restrict to idempotent summands. Each simple perverse summand T belongs to that additive category after a shift. Therefore End_R^*(Y_T)=Ext_G^*(T,T). For perverse T the heart orthogonality gives Hom_DG(T,T[m])=0 for m<0, so this algebra has no negative degrees; its degree-zero part is the division algebra End(T). Thus Y_T is indecomposable. The same additive equivalence exhausts all indecomposable projective shift orbits. The algebraic maximal-tail supplier already proves every simple R-module absolutely simple; a division degree-zero endomorphism algebra of a projective cover injects into its simple-head scalar ring, so End_R^0(Y_T)=k. This proves the essential positive-End property without VV4.8 augmentation/formality and without relying on a generalized geometric canonical comparison.\nBy the separately proved generic projective-duality supplier every projective orbit has a unique #-self-dual representative P_b. Put x_b=gamma^-1[P_b]. It is integral and bar fixed. The exact Hom/tensor comparison for a self-dual P gives B_L(x_b,x_b)=h(P_b,P_b)=1+q N[[q]], since the geometric End property is unchanged by grading shifts. Dividing by C_beta=1 moduloq gives B_K(x_b,x_b) in1+q Z[[q]]. The general QG5 half norm criterion therefore places x_b in the q0 crystal lattice. Bar fixes it, so it also lies in the actual bar chart; integral balanced globalization writes x_b as a finite Z-linear combination of lower global vectors. Their residue Gram matrix is the identity; norm residue1 forces the sum of coefficient squares to be1. Thus x_b is exactly plus or minus one lower global vector. Distinct projective shift orbits are independent and have the same finite weight cardinality as the global basis by the integral K_0 isomorphism, so they exhaust this signed set.\nThe new positive divided-string leading-term supplier removes every minus sign using its integral LEFT-string ideal equality, coefficient1 projective adjunction and the general adapted LEFT global recursion from1. It retains the full symmetric claim and does not use batch8's finite-ADE canonical-comparison item. The based quotient then follows from the general QG5 zero/survival projection. All algebraic steps and this conditional deduction are local; the exact semisimple quiver-flag Ext realization remains the genuine held geometric result.",
